Thinking back, I realize the cause of this issue. I had recently removed the explicit `spring-boot-starter-webmvc` dependency declaration from `task-web/pom.xml`. My assumption was that 
this dependency would be automatically inherited from the parent POM. However, it turns out that `spring-boot-starter-webmvc` isn't actually defined in the `dependencyManagement` section 
of our root `pom.xml`. This means that while the parent POM might manage *other* things, it's not providing a default for this particular starter, leading to the compilation problems in 
the submodule.

So, my plan to rectify this is straightforward:

First, I need to **add the `spring-boot-starter-webmvc` dependency to the `dependencyManagement` section of the root `pom.xml`**. This is the crucial step to ensure that all submodules, 
including `task-web`, can properly inherit and use the correct version of Spring Boot Web MVC without needing individual declarations.

Once that's in place, I'll **re-run `mvn clean install`**. This will allow me to confirm that the build now succeeds without those pesky compilation errors.

After I've got a clean build, the next logical step is to **re-run `osv-scanner`**. My goal here is to verify that any vulnerabilities that might have been related to the missing or 
